             “PVVNL”) is aggrieved by an order of the National Company Law Appellate
             Tribunal (hereinafter, “NCLAT”)1 which rejected its appeal against an order of the
             National Company Law Tribunal, Allahabad (hereinafter, “NCLT”/ “Adjudicating
             Authority”),2 which allowed an application directing the District Magistrate and
             Tehsildar, Muzaffarnagar to immediately release property (which was previously
             attached at the request of the appellant) in favour of the liquidator of the
             respondent Raman Ispat Pvt. Ltd. (hereinafter, “corporate debtor”) for enabling
             its sale, and after realisation of its value, for distributing the proceeds in
             accordance with the provisions of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016
             (hereinafter, “IBC” / “Code”).
