</p>
<blockquote id="blockquote_99">          <span class="citetext" data-sentiment="Pos" data-docid="137543007" id="span_107">“When two words of different import are used in a statute, in two consecutive
          provisions, it would be difficult to maintain that they are used in the same
          sense…”

      This idea is reflected in a subsequent judgment in <a href="/doc/137543007/" id="a_211">Brihan Mumbai
Mahanagarpalika &amp; Anr. v. Willington Sports Club &amp; Ors.37</a></span>

